			"text":"- [Lecture 2 - Resonance II](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TcvY8Nt0ZGA&list=PLUl4u3cNGP62FPGcyFJkzhqq9c5cHCK32&index=3&ab_channel=MITOpenCourseWare)\n\t- [Q factor (Wikipedia)](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Q_factor)\n\t- [Whispering Gallery Modes ( Wikipedia)](https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Whispering-gallery_wave)\n\t- A comparison between a 2-level system and the QHO. The two systems behave the same in the approximation of weak driving.\n\t- He said that if one excites a QHO, naturally states will \"leak\" to higher levels. This allegedly happens when the driving is not weak and the approximation between the two system no longer holds.\n\t- Two level system - can be saturated, a QHO can be driven to arbitrarily high energies.",
